        "original_id": "e40ed6a1-393b-591e-a8fd-5ab01518966b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Disporum, Boltonia, Disporum viridescens\n- Concepts: plant genera, species, geographic distribution, sunflower family\n\nFacts:\n- Disporum, commonly known as fairy bells, is a genus of about 20 species of perennial flowering plants.\n- Disporum is found in Asia from northern India to Japan, south to Indonesia, and north into the Russian Far East.\n- Boltonia is a genus of plants in the sunflower family.\n- Boltonia is native primarily to North America, with one species in eastern Asia.\n- Disporum viridescens is a species of flowering plant in the genus Disporum.",
